\"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"duplicate","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Duplicate of stinky-blushing-gelding, which was filed first for the same failure. The verified root cause and plan from this ticket are moved there.","timestamp":1795205696167050001}],"completion_expectation":"disposition","created_at":1795205582092611001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"41e91eab-8958-406b-bd80-c810664cc699","relation":"duplicates","target_id":"4020-ce89-21ef-431d"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nAn unsandboxed, slot-capped local `make verify` (worktree w05-fieldmouse, log `.rebar/scratch/05f74084-win/verify2-fieldmouse.log`, Nov 20 2026, load average about 30) failed `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py::test_gerrit_internal_webhook_does_not_need_unsupported_plugin_header` with `+++ Timeout +++ pytest-timeout expired after 3.0s` and a worker crash. CI passes it. The same three tests also expired in the 5 sandboxed runs of the same night, where the dumped main-thread stack was inside `tests/_isolation.py:_git_probe_once` called from the autouse `_no_repo_commits` fixture in `tests/conftest.py`.\n\n## Root cause (verified)\n`test_webhook_auth_rejection_is_visible_on_health`, `test_gerrit_internal_webhook_does_not_need_unsupported_plugin_header` and `test_gerrit_internal_webhook_requires_the_gerrit_service_peer` carry `@pytest.mark.timeout(3)`. The pyproject policy sets no `timeout_func_only`, so the 3 s budget covers setup and teardown too. The autouse `_no_repo_commits` fixture runs `git rev-parse HEAD` on the checkout in setup and again in teardown, each bounded by `GIT_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` (5) times `GIT_PROBE_ATTEMPTS` (3) in `tests/_isolation.py`. On a loaded host those two git starts alone exceed 3 s, so the marker kills the worker before the test body runs.\n\nDeterministic reproduction (Nov 20 2026, sandboxed shell, origin/main 8e1d15e664f): a PATH `git` shim that sleeps 1.6 s before exec-ing the real git makes `pytest -m \"\" tests/unit/test_review_bot.py -k \"webhook_auth_rejection_is_visible_on_health or gerrit_internal_webhook\"` print `+++ Timeout +++` during the setup phase every run; with the shim set to 0 s the same 3 tests pass in 2.79 s.\n\nThe same defect was fixed for one test in 530b0896eee (`test_lifespan_is_safe_by_default_without_per_test_stubs`, 3 s to 30 s), and `tests/unit/test_timeout_budget_headroom.py` guards only that one test by name, so its 3 siblings kept the 3 s marker.\n\n## Approach\nFix the class, not the 3 instances: a per-test timeout marker must not be tighter than the autouse isolation guard's own bounded cost.\n- In `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py`, change the three `@pytest.mark.timeout(3)` markers to `@pytest.mark.timeout(30)` with a one-line comment naming the reason (the marker wraps the autouse git probes). The tests carry no wall-clock assertion of their own to keep; their hang protection stays, at 30 s instead of 3 s.\n- In `tests/unit/test_timeout_budget_headroom.py`, replace `test_review_bot_lifespan_marker_covers_autouse_setup` (one named test) with a whole-tree AST census: every literal `pytest.mark.timeout(N)` under `tests/` must satisfy `N >= 2 * GIT_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS * GIT_PROBE_ATTEMPTS` (30 s today), importing both constants from `tests/_isolation.py` so the floor follows the guard if the guard changes. The failure message names each offending file, line and value.\n- No product code, config key, environment variable or flag changes.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_timeout_budget_headroom.py`\n\n## Testing\n- Before the change, the new census test fails naming the 3 review-bot markers (run recorded on this ticket); after, it passes.\n- Under the 1.6 s git shim the 3 review-bot tests pass after the change (run recorded here); with no shim they still pass.\n- Edge: the census reads both decorator markers and `pytestmark = pytest.mark.timeout(N)` assignments, and ignores non-literal arguments.\n- `make verify` through the shared verify slot passes on the change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No literal `pytest.mark.timeout(N)` under `tests/` is below the autouse git-probe bound, enforced by a census test in `tests/unit/test_timeout_budget_headroom.py` that derives its floor from `tests/_isolation.py`.\n- [ ] The 3 review-bot webhook tests pass under the 1.6 s-per-start git shim, with the run recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes on the change, and Gerrit gives Verified +1.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"e4ac2a34-25d4-4a1b-9901-95dc51d42016","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"9735-46ee-26b7-4822","ticket_type":"bug","title":"3 s timeout markers on review-bot webhook tests expire inside the autouse git probes on a loaded host","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c1426591-765f-416e-84ed-1d51ca6832db","41e91eab-8958-406b-bd80-c810664cc699","18511991-ed81-4e9e-91f7-7932b76a9497","e4ac2a34-25d4-4a1b-9901-95dc51d42016","4c5a3c22-a782-4dca-99e2-be34da957c3d"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795205794081619002,"uuid":"3397612c-8865-44d3-b33a-3210ba14384a"}